{"acceptance_length": 5.393939393939394, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 10, 4, 13, 6, 1, 2, 2, 3, 1, 3, 6, 3, 1, 4, 2, 2, 1, 6, 1, 8, 12, 3, 2, 10, 7, 11, 12, 3, 5, 3, 3, 1, 2, 2, 6, 4, 1, 2, 5, 4, 2, 5, 2, 6, 3, 2, 3, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 6, 15, 16, 15, 16, 16, 8, 16, 15, 14, 3, 1, 5], "accepted_draft_lengths": [2, 9, 3, 12, 5, 0, 1, 1, 2, 0, 2, 5, 2, 0, 3, 1, 1, 0, 5, 0, 7, 11, 2, 1, 9, 6, 10, 11, 2, 4, 2, 2, 0, 1, 1, 5, 3, 0, 1, 4, 3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 2, 1, 2, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 5, 14, 15, 14, 15, 15, 7, 15, 14, 13, 2, 0, 4], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 21618323456, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 21618317312, "benchmark": "mbpp", "completion": "Here's a correct implementation of the `comb_sort` function that satisfies all the given assertions:\n\n```python\ndef comb_sort(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                swapped = True\n\n    return arr\n```\n\n### Explanation:\n- **Comb Sort** is a variation of Bubble Sort that improves performance by comparing elements that are far apart.\n- The `gap` starts as the length of the list and is reduced by a shrink factor (typically 1.3) in each iteration.\n- The process continues until the gap is 1 and no swaps are made, indicating the list is sorted.\n\n### Test Cases:\n```python\nassert comb_sort([5, 15, 37, 25, 79]) == [5, 15, 25, 37, 79]\nassert comb_sort([41, 32, 15, 19, 22]) == [15, 19, 22, 32, 41]\nassert comb_sort([99, 15, 13, 47]) == [13, 15, 47, 99]\n```\n\nAll assertions will pass with this implementation.", "decode_seconds": 2.4273176258429885, "draft_calls": 66, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 200, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "ebbaf846258aa17f4c36496d3190e82add4d5ed74acdce2afba74d1ec80af5